* MUX509 dual 4:1 analog multiplexer (U24), behavioral, written for this
* project. Not a model of the manufacturer, who publishes none for this part.
*   On-resistance: the datasheet gives 125 ohm typical with +/-15 V and
*   235 ohm typical, 340 ohm at most with a single 12 V supply; with +12 V
*   and -4 V it gives nothing. The parameter ron is 250 ohm by default
*   (estimate) and the benches sweep 125 ohm to 430 ohm (specification,
*   section 4.3).
*   Capacitance of a drain with its channel on: 6.7 pF (datasheet).
*   Transition time from address to the new channel: 92 ns typical
*   (datasheet, page 1). The old channel opens first: 50 ns is an
*   assumption, the part breaks before it makes.
*   Logic threshold of the address and enable inputs: 1.4 V (assumption
*   between the usual limits of 0.8 V and 2.0 V).
*   Not modelled: leakage, charge injection, the capacitance of an open
*   channel, the dependence of the on-resistance on the signal level.
* Pins in the order of the package: A0 EN VSS S1A S2A S3A S4A DA DB S4B S3B
* S2B S1B VDD GND A1.
.subckt MUX509 a0 en vss s1a s2a s3a s4a da db s4b s3b s2b s1b vdd gnd a1
+ params: ron=250 roff=1e12 cdon=6.7p ttran=92n toff=50n vth=1.4
* ngspice puts the text of a brace expression into a behavioral source as it
* is, so a sum has to be a parameter of its own before it is multiplied.
.param goff={1/roff}
.param gadd={1/ron - 1/roff}
Ba0 b0 0 V = 0.5*(1 + tanh((v(a0,gnd) - {vth})/0.05))
Ba1 b1 0 V = 0.5*(1 + tanh((v(a1,gnd) - {vth})/0.05))
Ben be 0 V = 0.5*(1 + tanh((v(en,gnd) - {vth})/0.05))
Bs1 q1 0 V = v(be)*(1 - v(b1))*(1 - v(b0))
Bs2 q2 0 V = v(be)*(1 - v(b1))*v(b0)
Bs3 q3 0 V = v(be)*v(b1)*(1 - v(b0))
Bs4 q4 0 V = v(be)*v(b1)*v(b0)
Xc1 q1 c1 MUX509_CTL ttran={ttran} toff={toff}
Xc2 q2 c2 MUX509_CTL ttran={ttran} toff={toff}
Xc3 q3 c3 MUX509_CTL ttran={ttran} toff={toff}
Xc4 q4 c4 MUX509_CTL ttran={ttran} toff={toff}
Bw1a s1a da I = v(s1a,da)*({goff} + {gadd}*v(c1))
Bw2a s2a da I = v(s2a,da)*({goff} + {gadd}*v(c2))
Bw3a s3a da I = v(s3a,da)*({goff} + {gadd}*v(c3))
Bw4a s4a da I = v(s4a,da)*({goff} + {gadd}*v(c4))
Bw1b s1b db I = v(s1b,db)*({goff} + {gadd}*v(c1))
Bw2b s2b db I = v(s2b,db)*({goff} + {gadd}*v(c2))
Bw3b s3b db I = v(s3b,db)*({goff} + {gadd}*v(c3))
Bw4b s4b db I = v(s4b,db)*({goff} + {gadd}*v(c4))
Cda da gnd {cdon}
Cdb db gnd {cdon}
* While the part breaks before it makes, both outputs float. These two
* resistors keep the matrix of the solver regular; they draw 50 pA at 5 V
* and are no statement about the leakage of the part.
Rda da gnd 1e11
Rdb db gnd 1e11
Rvd vdd gnd 1e9
Rvs vss gnd 1e9
.ends MUX509

* Control of one channel: closes ttran after its selection, opens toff after
* the selection ends.
* The product of the two delayed copies is their logical and, without the
* corners of a min or a max, at which the solver can stop.
.subckt MUX509_CTL q c params: ttran=92n toff=50n
Rq q qf 1k
Cq qf 0 2p
Xon qf xon DLY td={ttran}
Xoff qf xoff DLY td={toff}
Bc c 0 V = v(xon)*v(xoff)
.ends MUX509_CTL
